# Strumming: Boom-Chick (repertoire plan: st-boom-chick). An original country-style study.
# G, C, D7, G, four bars each. Boom: a bass note on beats 1 and 3. Chick: a down-strum of
# strings 4 to 1 on beats 2 and 4. Bass notes: G alternates string 6 fret 3 (G) and the open
# string 4 (D); C alternates string 5 fret 3 (C) and string 6 fret 3 (G), finger 3 moving between
# them; D7 alternates the open string 4 (D) and the open string 5 (A). Shapes G (320003),
# C (x32010), D7 (xx0212); G is fingered 3-2-4 here so fingers 3 and 2 slide across for C.
# Bar 4 walks up into C with a bass note on every beat: G, then G A B, and C lands on beat 1
# of bar 5. Written as notes rather than slashes so you can see exactly which strings to hit.
title: Strumming: Boom-Chick
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original strumming study in the country style
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: boom-chick, alternating bass, country, walk-up
tempo: 88
time: 4/4
key: G

